{"comparisons":[],"failures":[],"frontier":[{"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["The expressly US-worded liquidity example is read literally; Canada's inclusion still governs the general Transition readiness expectation.","The Boolean result evaluates only the selected liquidity control within scope and does not determine overall compliance."],"citations":[{"quote":"Reviewing their liquidity risk management practices and ensuring the necessary funding is available for settling US securities transactions on time.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996"},{"quote":"For cross-currency transactions, given that the standard settlement cycle for foreign-exchange transactions remains at T+2, LCs should be mindful of potential liquidity mismatches and settlement failures arising from the different settlement cycles for US securities and foreign-exchange transactions;","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996"},{"quote":"The reference to the Transition in this circular includes the transition in the US and Canada.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399"}],"distinction":"The specific liquidity example expressly tests US transactions. Canadian readiness remains relevant under the general provision, but is not an additional condition of this selected test. The strongest uncertainty is how the broader defined Transition interacts with repeated US-specific wording.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed entity is a licensed corporation.","name":"is_lc","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The LC's business involves US securities settlements affected by the Transition.","name":"us_affected","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The LC's business involves Canadian securities settlements affected by the Transition.","name":"canada_affected","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498","d2ccfaeb3eb4b