":"Reviewing their liquidity risk management practices and ensuring the necessary funding is available for settling US securities transactions on time.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996"},{"quote":"2 The settlement cycle in Canada will transition to T+1 on 27 May 2024. The reference to the Transition in this circular includes the transition in the US and Canada.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399"}],"distinction":"An LC affected only in Canada enters scope, and an LC affected in both markets must satisfy liquidity readiness for both. This gains support from the defined Transition and inclusive readiness introduction, but requires extending the expressly US-worded example; that extension is the strongest uncertainty.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed entity is a licensed corporation.","name":"is_lc","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The LC's business involves US securities settlements affected by the Transition.","name":"us_affected","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The LC's business involves Canadian securities settlements affected by the Transition.","name":"canada_affected","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"For the affected US business, liquidity practices have been reviewed, necessary funding is available for timely securities settlement, and any cross-currency cycle mismatch and resulting failure risk have been considered.","name":"us_liquidity_ready","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"For the affected Canadian business, liquidity practices have been reviewed, necessary funding is available for timely securities settlement, and any cross-currency cycle mismatch and resulting failure risk have been considered.","name":"canada_liquidity_ready","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and (if us_affected us_liquidity_ready true) (if canada_affected canada_liquidity_ready true))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_lc (or us_affected canada_affected))"},"local_id":"liquidity_transition_wide","questions":["Is extending the liquidity example to Canada justified by the defined term despite the specific US references?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] For an LC with affected US or Canadian settlement business, true means the selected Transition-wide liquidity readiness expectation is met for each affected market: liquidity review, timely funding, and consideration of relevant cross-currency mismatch risks. Canada transitions on 2024-05-27 and the US on 2024-05-28; the FX cycle remains T+2.","subject":"LC liquidity readiness: Transition-wide geographic reach"},"reason":"LEGACY_FAMILY_RESERVATION"},{"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["Outcome expectations and optional implementation suggestions retain their different modalities.","Adequacy and timeliness require assessment against the LC's relevant operations; no fixed headcount or training duration is supplied."],"citations":[{"quote":"Ensuring the availability of staff to complete the post-trade settlement processes within the shortened timeframe.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448"},{"quote":"LCs may consider adjusting their staff’s work shifts, extending working hours or arranging evening or morning duties in conjunction with automating their operational processes to enable timely trade settlements.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448"},{"quote":"Adequate training should be provided to enable relevant staff to effectively perform their duties under the shortened settlement cycle;","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448"},{"quote":"3 Including trade allocation, confirmation and affirmation.","unit_i