ment cycle.","name":"canada_short_cycle_transaction","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The LC has reviewed its liquidity risk management practices relevant to the selected transaction.","name":"liquidity_practices_reviewed","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The necessary funding is available to settle the selected transaction by its applicable settlement deadline, taking account of any cross-currency timing mismatch.","name":"timely_funding_available","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and liquidity_practices_reviewed timely_funding_available)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_lc (or us_short_cycle_transaction canada_short_cycle_transaction))"},"local_id":"l2","questions":["Is extending the bullet to Canada intended, or does the footnote expand only provisions using the defined Transition?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] For the selected transaction-level liquidity control, an LC handling either a US or Canadian transaction under the shortened cycle satisfies the proposed control when it has reviewed relevant liquidity practices and ensured timely funding.","subject":"Geographic reach of the specific liquidity control"},"reason":"LEGACY_FAMILY_RESERVATION"},{"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["The reading expresses the circular's supervisory expectation without assigning a statutory sanction.","Adequacy is assessed for the LC's relevant operations and personnel."],"citations":[{"quote":"Ensuring the availability of staff to complete the post-trade settlement processes within the shortened timeframe.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448"},{"quote":"LCs may consider adjusting their staff’s work shifts, extending working hours or arranging evening or morning duties in conjunction with automating their operational processes to enable timely trade settlements.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448"},{"quote":"Adequate training should be provided to enable relevant staff to effectively perform their duties under the shortened settlement cycle;","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448"},{"quote":"3 Including trade allocation, confirmation and affirmation.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567"},{"quote":"These include enhancing their operational processes, technological infrastructure and systems as well as staffing arrangements where appropriate.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498"}],"distinction":"An LC with sufficient existing coverage and adequate training can satisfy this control without changing shifts, extending hours or introducing automation. Making any listed method mandatory lacks support in 'may consider'. The uncertain attachment of 'where appropriate' affects enhancement choices but does not clearly displace staff availability or training.","family":"modality","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed entity is a licensed corporation addressed by the circular.","name":"is_lc","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The LC has relevant post-trade settlement processes affected by the US or Canadian shortened cycle.","name":"affected_settlement_processes","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Staff are available to complete all relevant post-trade settlement processes within the applicable shortened timeframe.","name":"sufficient_staff_available","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Relevant staff have received adequate training to perform their duties effectively under the shortened cycle.","name":"adequate_training_provided","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and sufficient_staff_available adequate_training_provided)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_lc affected_settlement_processes)"},"local_id":"l3","questions":["What staffing coverage and training evidence establish adequacy for the relevant processes and time zones?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] The selected staffing-readiness control is satisfied when sufficient staff are available within the shortened timeframe and relevant staff receive adequate training. The listed scheduling and automation measures remain discretionary means.","subject":"Staff availability, training and optional implementation measures"},"reason":"LEGACY_FAMILY_RESERVATION"},{"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["Client selection turns on potential effects of either country's transition, without requiring a realised settlement failure.","Proactive preparation implies advance engagement but does not supply a fixed number of days."],"citations":[{"quote":"Proactively engaging and communicating with their clients who are potentially affected by the Transition in order to raise their awareness and facilitate their preparations for a smooth transition.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u5.1916"},{"quote":"The reference to the Transition in this circular includes the transition in the US and Canada.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399"}],"distinction":"A client potentially affected only by Canada's transition is included. Restricting communication to US clients or clients already experiencing failures would conflict with the express definition and 'potentially affected'. No source-supported rival narrows the control that way.","family":"scope","formalization":null,"local_id":"l4","questions":["Which clients are potentially affected, and how early must engagement occur to facilitate their preparations?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] The selected client-preparation control calls for proactive engagement and communication with potentially affected clients concerning either transition, directed at awareness and preparation. The packet does not supply measurable content or timing thresholds for an executable test.","subject":"Affected-client communication"},"reason":"LEGACY_FAMILY_RESERVATION"}],"initial":{"alternatives":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Interpreted as the US transition date and business-day settlement context, read with the Canada footnote.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0"},{"reason":"Interpreted as LC-wide impact assessment and proportionate operational measures.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498"},{"reason":"Supplies the readiness expectation governing the operational list.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879"},{"reason":"Supports competing geographic readings of the selected liquidity control and distinguishes FX settlement.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996"},{"reason":"Interpreted as staff availability and training expectations with optional implementation measures.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448"},{"reason":"Interpreted as communication with potentially affected clients.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u5.1916"},{"reason":"Identifies a separate fund-management actor category; considerable US exposure is emphasis, not an express eligibility threshold.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u6.2116"},{"reason":"Fund-specific impact assessment is outside the selected LC operational control; it does not automatically apply to every LC.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u7.2267"},{"reason":"Fund-specific arrangements and investor-interest standard require separate interpretation; examples do not make additional staffing universally mandatory.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u8.2499"},{"reason":"Fund-specific early alerts and remedial action are outside the selected control and cannot be imported into the LC client-communication provision.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u9.2771"},{"reason":"Describes SFC monitoring rather than an LC operational requirement.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u10.2996"},{"reason":"Departmental attribution, not an operative control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u11.3083"},{"reason":"Institutional attribution, not an operative control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u12.3172"},{"reason":"Institutional signature, not an operative control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u13.3290"},{"reason":"Provides illustrative, non-exhaustive securities examples.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u14.3336"},{"reason":"Expressly includes Canada in the defined Transition and supplies its distinct date.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399"},{"reason":"Provides non-exhaustive examples of post-trade settlement processes.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"LCs are the actors for the selected operational provisions. General Transition readiness includes Canada; whether the expressly US-worded liquidity bullet extends identically to Canada supports a narrower and a broader reading. Fund managers have additional, separate provisions.","source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u6.2116","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Transition expressly includes the US and Canada. Securities and post-trade processes are illustrated with 'Such as' and 'Including'; neither list is exhaustive. These definitions do not expressly replace every occurrence of 'US securities' with both jurisdictions.","source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u14.3336","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"'Where appropriate' qualifies operational enhancements, with its precise grammatical reach unresolved. It does not clearly exempt LCs from assessment or negate the specific staff-availability expectation. FX T+2 is a distinct cycle, not an exception excusing timely securities funding.","source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"'Should', 'ensuring' and 'should be provided' express supervisory expectations; 'may consider' preserves discretion over staffing methods. The packet does not establish the legal consequences of non-performance.","source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"Canada transitions on 2024-05-27 and the US on 2024-05-28. T+1 and T+2 concern business-day cycles, not calendar-day arithmetic. Readiness and client preparation are anticipatory, but no exact assessment or communication deadline is supplied.","source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u5.1916","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The operational bullets depend on the LC readiness introduction; footnotes qualify the opening terms. Application requires business exposure, applicable settlement timing and professional adequacy judgments. No external dependency text, market calendar or operational cutoff is supplied.","source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u14.3336","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567"],"status":"PROPOSED"}],"questions":["Does the Canada-inclusive definition extend the specific US-worded funding bullet to Canadian transactions, or do Canadian funding arrangements fall under the general appropriateness and readiness expectations?","What evidence establishes appropriate measures, adequate training, time